# Client conventions

Single-page app — **no React Router**. State lives in `App.jsx`; children are presentational.

## Components

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/App.jsx` | State, `handleSend` / `handleReset`, layout |
| `src/components/RecipientList.jsx` | Manual add or CSV/Excel/PDF import |
| `src/utils/extractEmails.js` | Parse emails from uploaded list files |
| `src/components/EmailComposer.jsx` | Subject, body, attachments (drag/drop) |
| `src/components/SendStatus.jsx` | Per-recipient sent/failed results |

## Send flow (`App.jsx`)

- Gate: ≥1 recipient, non-empty subject & body, not `sending`
- Body: newlines → `<br/>` before send
- `recipients` = `JSON.stringify(array)`; files field name `attachments`
- `fetch('/api/send')` — do not set `Content-Type` (browser sets multipart boundary)
- `SENDER_EMAIL` is display-only; actual From is server SMTP user

## UI notes

- Styles: `src/index.css` with CSS variables (dark theme, `--accent: #6c63ff`)
- Client attachment UX: ~25 MB per file; accept pdf/doc/xls/images/zip
- Max 10 attachments enforced on **server** only — keep client in mind if adding limits
